## The authority this verdict rests on

**X960 platform support TPS** (`wiki.atlnz.lc/awpwiki/index.php?title=X960_platform_support_TPS`,
last modified 2026-10-19), fetched at triage and quoted in the campaign queue:

| TPS row | feature | supported | comment, verbatim |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **236** | **Management Stacking** | **No** | *"Management Stacking is not necessary as these units support VCS"* |

Per the standing method note `review-feature-docs-before-testing`, **a TPS row of `No` is read
off as UNSUPPORTED, with the TPS as the evidence.** It is not a bench request and not a bench
gap: the product deliberately does not offer the feature, because the same need is met by
Virtual Chassis Stacking (VCS).

`logged-output.md` section 1 defines UNSUPPORTED as *"the platform does not support what the
case tests"*, and records that an UNSUPPORTED case does not stop the test set being a PASS.

