## The measurement -- what the DUT itself says about stacking

Commands run with `tools/tb ckcon tb277 mgmt1159 u2 115200 ...` (read-only) and
`tools/tb qmark tb277 mgmt1159 u2 115200 ...` (read-only `?` help probe, which types the prefix
and `?` with **no CR**, prints the completions, then clears the line with Ctrl-U; its self-test
confirmed first that nothing gets executed).

### 1. The DUT agrees with the TPS: stacking hardware is disabled

```
awplus#show stack
% Warning: Stacking is currently disabled
Virtual Chassis Stacking summary information

ID   Pending ID  MAC address        Priority  Status  Role
1    -           e01a.ead4.7043     128       Ready   Active Master

Operational Status                 Stacking hardware disabled
Stack MAC address                  e01a.ead4.7043
```

```
awplus#show stack detail
% Warning: Stacking is currently disabled
Virtual Chassis Stacking detailed information

Stack Status:
------------------------------------------------------------------
Operational Status                      Stacking hardware disabled
Management VLAN ID                      0
Management VLAN subnet address          192.168.255.0
Virtual Chassis ID                      403 (0x193)
Virtual MAC address                     Disabled
Disabled Master Monitoring              Enabled
Mixed Mode                              Disabled

Stack member 1:
------------------------------------------------------------------
ID                                      1
Pending ID                              -
MAC address                             e01a.ead4.7043
Last role change                        Tue Oct 20 20:56:51 2026
Product type                            AT-x960-56YSQ
Role                                    Active Master
Status                                  Ready
Priority                                128
Host name                               awplus
S/W version auto synchronization        On
Resiliency link status                  Not configured
```

```
awplus#show stack resiliencylink
% Stacking is currently disabled, please save the config and reboot after enabling stacking.
```

Read together: **one member, ID 1, Ready, Active Master**; Virtual Chassis ID **403 (0x193)**;
**Operational Status `Stacking hardware disabled`**; resiliency link **Not configured**. The
DUT is a standalone unit whose VCS hardware is switched off.

🔴 **A deviation from the TPS worth recording.** The X960 TPS's **Default Configuration**
section states *"Stacking is enabled by default"*. **This DUT reads `Stacking hardware
disabled`.** The two statements disagree. This is not what the case is about and it does not
change the verdict (row 236 is `No` either way), but it is a documented mismatch between the
product's stated default and the unit on this bench, and it is reported to the Test Engineer.
It is also possible that this unit's `flash:/default.cfg` simply never carried `stack enable`;
the running-config captured in `swi_d.cfg` beside this log contains **no** `stack` line at all,
so nothing in the configuration is switching it off -- the hardware is reported off with the
feature at its configured default.

### 2. What exists INSTEAD: the VCS configuration surface

The reason the TPS gives for row 236 being `No` -- *"these units support VCS"* -- is directly
visible in the CLI. Config mode, `?` probe only, nothing executed, nothing created:

```
awplus(config)#stack ?
  <1-8>                       A specific stack member ID
  all                         all stack member configuration
  disabled-master-monitoring  Enables the resiliency-link monitoring when the
                              device is a Disabled-Master.
  enable                      Enable VCS hardware
  management                  VCS management VLAN configuration
  mixed-mode                  Set this stack member to be compatible with
                              other products
  resiliencylink              Resiliency link configuration for the stack
  virtual-chassis-id          VCS virtual chassis id
  virtual-mac                 Enable the virtual MAC address feature

awplus(config)#stack 1 ?
  priority                   Change the specified stack member priority value
  renumber                   Change the existing stack member ID
  software-auto-synchronize  stack member software version auto
                             synchronization

awplus(config)#stack management ?
  subnet  Subnet address of the VCS management VLAN
  vlan    VCS management VLAN

awplus(config)#stack enable ?
  <cr>
```

and in exec mode:

```
awplus#show stack ?
  detail          Detailed information display
  full-debug      Complete detailed debug information
  resiliencylink  Stack resiliency link information
```

So the platform offers a **complete VCS surface** -- enable the hardware, a management VLAN and
subnet, a virtual chassis id, a virtual MAC, a resiliency link, per-member priority, renumbering,
software auto-synchronisation and mixed mode. **That is the mechanism this platform provides in
place of Management Stacking**, exactly as TPS row 236 says.

### 3. What this case WOULD need if VCS were to be exercised, and why this bench cannot give it

A real VCS exercise needs **two stackable units of the same product**, both with
`stack enable` written and both reloaded (the DUT itself says so:
`% Stacking is currently disabled, please save the config and reboot after enabling stacking`),
plus a stacking link between them. On tb277:

- **swi_b is a different model** -- AT-x960-28YSQ against the DUT's AT-x960-56YSQ -- and
  `platforms/x960.md` section 1 records that the two models do not share a switching core. It is
  not a stack partner for the DUT.
- **swi_a would have to be reloaded**, and the session constraint for 2026-10-21 forbids
  rebooting or power-cycling swi_a outright (it reads `Current boot image : Not set` and may not
  come back). It is also an AT-x950 GEN2-52XSTQm, a different product again.
- Enabling VCS on the DUT alone would need a `write` plus a reload and would produce a
  one-member "stack", which is what the DUT already reports. It would prove nothing about
  Management Stacking and would risk the campaign's inherited bench state.

**No bench change is requested**, because a bench change could not turn this verdict into a PASS:
the feature under test is one the product states it does not implement. A second
AT-x960-56YSQ on its own console and PDU outlet would let a *VCS* case be written -- a different
case from this one.

