## Teardown and the after-run checks

**There is nothing to tear down: this case changed no device state.** Every command it issued
was a `show` or a `?` help probe. In particular, `platforms/x960.md` section 7F.6 records that
entering a config sub-mode and leaving without setting anything creates nothing; here not even
that happened -- `qmark.py` types the prefix and `?` with no carriage return and then clears the
line with Ctrl-U, and its self-test proved on this console that nothing is executed.

- **Console state, read from the box's own transcript** (`/tmp/mgmt1159/console-u2.log`), not
  from a tool's stdout: after the config-mode `?` probes, `tools/tb peek tb277 mgmt1159 u2
  115200` returned **`/dev/u2 TAIL: 'awplus#'`** -- the console is back at the privileged exec
  prompt, out of config mode. (One `?` probe was typed against the literal prefix `--`, an
  argument-parsing slip of mine; the device answered `% Unrecognized command`, the line was
  cleared by Ctrl-U and nothing was executed. Recorded here because it is in the transcript.)
- **u3 and u5 were not opened by this case.** The group's final console handling (`end`,
  `terminal no monitor`, `exit`) is done once at the end of group B, after T47192.
- **`show running-config` diff:** the running-config captured for `swi_d.cfg` at the start of
  this case is the running-config at the end of it; no configuration command was sent.
- The before-and-after bench probe for the group is recorded under the pre-run gate (exit 0
  MATCH); the group's closing probe is run after the last case.

